\ Bounded-memory regression for transient string results on the main task.
\
\ A string produced by #append or >string used to land on the context arena,
\ which is never reclaimed on the main task, so each of these loops grew
\ monotonically and exhausted the 4 MB cap set in the `.flags` sidecar
\ partway through. String and symbol payloads now carry refcounted heap
\ backings, so a dropped result is freed at the drop and both loops stay
\ flat.

20000 [ "hello, " "world" #append drop ] times
20000 [ 123456789 >string drop ] times

"flat" print-line
